2026-09-24 M0 config/quotas.yaml: model ids are defaults for the free tiers (gemini-2.5-flash-lite / gemini-2.5-flash, llama-3.3-70b); limits left null until Manzoor copies them (BRIEF §2.6 says never hard-code).
2026-09-24 M0 pytest markers: `snapshots` (needs network-fetched universe files) and `oldrepo` (needs the old doomberg checkout) are excluded from `make test` and run by verify M0-05 / M0-04, so the default suite never skips.
2026-09-24 M0 config/holdcos.yaml and config/cusip_overrides.yaml: created empty; BRIEF §4.2/§4.6 reference them but §2.3 does not list them.
2026-09-24 M0 guard: root manifests (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, web/package.json) are always checked for banned packages even though they are outside scan_paths; otherwise a banned dependency could be added without an import.
2026-09-24 M0 guard pit_rule: a "read" is SQL `from|join <table>` or ORM `.from('<table>')`/`.table('<table>')` in code files; db/migrations are exempt (DDL).
2026-09-24 M0 Makefile: migrate-dev and thesis-validate exit 1 with "arrives in M1/M6" until their modules exist, rather than pretending to succeed.
2026-09-24 M0 legacy Lab signals: L1-L6 defined in docs/DOOMBERG_AUDIT.md §5; weights 0 in config/weights.yaml pending Manzoor's confirmation (BRIEF §11.2).
2026-09-24 M0 .claude/settings.json: Appendix C checked against current Claude Code docs — `:*` prefix rules and the hook schema are valid; `MultiEdit` no longer exists (harmless in the matcher, kept verbatim). Added deny rules for the GitHub MCP merge tools (mcp__github__merge_pull_request, mcp__github__enable_pr_auto_merge): cloud threads merge through MCP, not `gh`, so `Bash(gh pr merge:*)` alone didn't enforce "never merge". `Bash(git push --force:*)` is order-sensitive (misses `git push origin x --force`); the real force-push control is branch protection on main (docs/SPEC_ISSUES.md 7).
2026-09-24 M0 scripts/protected_check.py: `git diff --name-only --no-renames` — without it, renaming a protected file away listed only the new path and passed with no label (found in M0 testing; regression tests in tests/guard/test_protected.py).
2026-09-24 M0 scripts/guard_hook.py: guard runs via `uv run --frozen` — a plain `uv run` after an edit to pyproject.toml re-locked uv.lock and installed the new dependency before the guard could flag it (found in M0 testing; regression test in tests/guard/test_hook.py).
2026-09-24 Manzoor: L1-L6 all go into the Signal Lab (weights stay 0 until the Lab proves them, §4.10.5); capex US seed keeps all 61 tickers; REITs stay in the US universe; the Signal Lab (M8) runs right after M4, before the web app (M7).
2026-09-24 M0 universe snapshots: SEC answered 429 "Request Rate Threshold Exceeded" to the cloud session's shared egress IP for ~25 min, then 200; both snapshots were fetched from the session. Added .github/workflows/universe.yml (fetch on a runner, commit to the branch; needs the SEC_USER_AGENT secret) as the fallback and for rebuilds. fetch_fixtures.py gained `--source sec|nse`.
2026-09-24 M0 capex seed India: E2E, STLTECH and HFCL are listed in NSE series BE (trade-for-trade), not EQ, so §1.3 keeps them out of the universe; listed with that reason in docs/UNIVERSE_ISSUES.md rather than moved into EQ.
2026-09-24 M0 scripts/guard_hook.py: `uv run` exits 1 when it can't sync (package index unreachable), which the hook read as a guard violation and blocked every edit. Exit 1 now counts only with the guard's summary line; otherwise the hook retries with the system interpreter (the guard needs only pyyaml). Regression test: tests/test_guard_hook_uv_failure.py.
2026-09-24 M1 db/migrations/0001_init.sql: §3 and Appendix F.2 DDL copied verbatim; deviations live in 0002/0003 so they stay auditable.
2026-09-24 M1 0002: ownership_q and corp_events get `filed_at timestamptz not null`. §3's point-in-time rule needs filed_at, and these two tables had none, so a 13F count or an 8-K event would have been visible from its quarter/event date (look-ahead). ownership_q keeps §3's key (company, quarter_end): a later revision replaces the row, so as_of() before the revision sees a gap, never the revised value. See SPEC_ISSUES 8.
2026-09-24 M1 access: RLS on every table with no policies, AND all privileges revoked from anon/authenticated, so an API-role query fails (M1-03 "fail") instead of returning an empty set. Roles anon/authenticated/service_role are created only if missing (no-op on Supabase).
2026-09-24 M1 display views (SPEC_ISSUES 6): 0003 adds fundamentals/ownership/insider_events/corp_events *_display_v with security_invoker=true (a default owner-rights view would let Supabase's anon role read around RLS). The web reads only these; tests/db/test_display_views.py fails if pipeline/ or scripts/ reference them.
2026-09-24 M1 dedupe: insider_events and corp_events get unique natural-key indexes (0002) and writers use `on conflict do nothing`; a `where not exists (select … from insider_events)` dedupe would itself be a PIT read outside pit.py (the guard flagged it).
2026-09-24 M1 CLAUDE.md "SQL only in db/migrations" read as "DDL only in db/migrations": repositories need DML. Exceptions: migrate.py's schema_migrations bookkeeping table and size_guard.py's temp probe tables (dropped in the same session).
2026-09-24 M1 as_of(W): W is a date = the end of W in UTC (filed_at < W+1 day 00:00 UTC), or an aware datetime = that instant (inclusive); naive datetimes and strings are rejected.
2026-09-24 M1 CI: python job gets a postgres:16 service (doom/doom) and runs make verify-m1 (includes M0).
2026-09-24 M1 local runs: this cloud environment's network policy blocks pypi.org/files.pythonhosted.org, so uv sync can't install deps in the session; SQL was checked with psql, Python with ruff + the guard, and the test suite runs in CI.
